e that makes sense and  you know of course you know Winston and  tracer were friends and they went on all  these adventures and you know that's  that's sort of the organic process that  we've been going with for overwatch you  know our hope has been that these  episodes we've been working on which is  just one of the funnest projects we've  done in years that they fill in enough  not necessarily like you know the the  perfect scope of the world but are just  these very distinct short stories that  kind of feel any like ah I get it I get  the tone I get this world as it's you  know we're I think next week the the  next episode comes out which is based on  Widowmaker and it's it's it's much  darker than the first one it's almost  the extreme of the gamut of tone and  theme that overwatch is inherently based  on so I'm totally fascinated to see what  people think and how does that fill out  their picture of the world you know more  than just Widowmaker or whoever's  involved in that episode how does it  make them feel and what kind of new  questions does it get them to ask you  know about this unfolding tapestry  that's kind of what's fun about it you  know it doesn't feel tracked it doesn't  feel like we're on a you know it's it's  just the highways completely open for us  to explore themes and ideas and it's  super liberating one thing we wanted to  try was what if we don't just fill in  all the blanks you know what if we don't  just give you a big timeline and say you  know here are all the big important  things that happen here are the you know  explicit interactions between the  characters that are in their history and  we want people to sort of experience  these different parts and to start to  form their own opinions like solve some  of these mysteries we put out there like  there's a certain sort of almost like a  collaboration that we're having with the  community therefore we we give them some  things we see what they're interested in  it might inspire us but I think that we  have a number of tools do this so  obviously we have the game world and  throughout the game world we're able to  put little hints in in the way that the  art is you know presented the way kind  of like the decorations that we put  around the map the things characters say  it's quite limited you know one or two  sentences back and forth but in that you  start to get the wave characters feel  about each other they can respond to  events that are happening in the  universe and we start to kind of peel  the layers off and show you what's going  on underneath the surface and that's it  thank you so much for watching the story  of overwatch a three-part series on  blizzards first new game world in 17  years we do hope you enjoyed this little  peek into how overwatch was crafted and  for continuing coverage of overwatch as  well as thousands of other video games  make sure you subscribe to this channel  or visit GameSpot comm thanks we'll see  you next time  armored over  okay  know what  you
 

